{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"scholars_lodge","model_identifier":"scholars_lodge","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# scholars_lodge\n\nScholar's Lodge: a timber cottage with a bright reading-room wing (big windows) and a little copper observatory dome with an open slot.\n\n- Footprint: 9 x 7 columns (144 x 112 units, 4.05 x 3.15 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -62..60, y 0..127, z -28..44 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 512, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 141, construction_0 74, construction_33 83, construction_66 112, ruined 88 (10 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- lodge: 112 x 128 x 64 centred at x 0, z 8\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `scholars_lodge_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `scholars_lodge_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_scholars_lodge` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_door` at (-24, 0, -33)\n"},"resolutio